{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mr6p3nheta6","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"bump geometry mismatch stride five mover cannot reach adjacency ls20","summary":"Run 26 (ARC healthy, player_colors=[9,12], per-run dedup fixed): bumps STILL 0 — bump_due_batches=21, bump_empty_batches=21, skip_reason 'all bump contexts already deduped (this run)'. ROOT CAUSE (design, not wiring): _bump_discovery/_bump_contexts assume UNIT-STEP adjacency contact — plan the player onto an empty cell distance-1 from an object, then step in. But ls20's player moves in STRIDES OF ±5 (ceiling program ACTION1-4 = ±5 translations, start ~(11,35)), so it can only occupy a sparse lattice of cells (offsets that are multiples of 5) and essentially NEVER lands adjacent to an arbitrary object -> _plan_to_cell returns None -> 'bump approach cell unreachable' -> object marked attempted, bump never fires. Every object skips the same way. IMPLICATION: for a stride-N mover, a 'bump'/contact is not stand-adjacent-then-step; it is a ±N move whose destination lands ON or whose path passes THROUGH an object (collision mid-stride). The interaction/contact model must match the movement quantum inferred from the world-model program (the per-action delta magnitude), not assume distance-1 adjacency. FIX DIRECTION (run 27 if pursued): derive the movement stride from the adopted program's step deltas; redefine bump targets as objects reachable/crossable by a single stride from a lattice-reachable cell; plan to the lattice cell whose next stride enters the object. 26 runs, 0 levels cleared; harness mechanically complete; this is the standing bump blocker. All fixes merged to main (head 8d791bdf region).","category":null,"tags":["arc-agi-3","ewm","bump-geometry","finding"],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-07-04T18:28:11.042Z","vec":[-0.09224893897771835,-0.07805624604225159,0.049747370183467865,-0.01844991371035576,0.024956243112683296,-0.017194747924804688,-0.02508097141981125,0.0428663715720176